From: KB2UKA <kb2uka80@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] fix(dts): j713: use ADT-proven MTP reset GPIOs

The J713 ADT provides reset functions below dockchannel-mtp/mtp-transport.
The multi-touch function targets SMC key gP1c and STM targets gP1d, both
through the smc-pmu provider. The Linux apple,smc-gpio driver encodes its
offset as two hexadecimal digits after gP, so these are pins 28 and 29.

Replace the inherited J413/J613 pins 8 and 24. Retain the existing polarity;
the key mapping alone does not independently prove the electrical polarity.

Credit: KB2UKA
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j713.dts | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j713.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j713.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j713.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j713.dts
@@ -102,4 +102,4 @@
 &mtp_hid {
-	apple,afe-reset-gpios = <&smc_gpio 8 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
-	apple,stm-reset-gpios = <&smc_gpio 24 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+	apple,afe-reset-gpios = <&smc_gpio 28 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+	apple,stm-reset-gpios = <&smc_gpio 29 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;

--
